# How `thunder-gptoss:latest` is built - the chat, medical, claims and
# consolidation model as of 2026-09-29.
#
# Recorded because the old `thunder-modelfile` was retired that day and this
# was the only live model with no recipe in the repo. Rebuild with:
#
#     ollama pull gpt-oss:20b
#     ollama create thunder-gptoss -f thunder-gptoss-modelfile
#
# Note what is NOT here: there is no SYSTEM block. Thunder's persona is sent as
# a system message by `app.py` (`SYSTEM_PROMPT`) on every request, so it can be
# changed without rebuilding the model. The old Mistral build baked its prompt
# in, which is why `thunder-modelfile` looks so different.
# Note what is ALSO not here: there is no TEMPLATE line, and that is
# deliberate. This file used to carry `TEMPLATE {{ .Prompt }}`, which is a bare
# passthrough - it would have handed the model one flat string with no roles
# and no tool block. It never reached the running model (verified 2026-09-29:
# the live thunder-gptoss template is byte-identical, sha256 a4c9919c..., to
# stock gpt-oss:20b's), so the recipe and the model had quietly diverged and
# only the recipe was wrong. Rebuilding from it would have destroyed the
# harmony format and with it every tool call. Omitting TEMPLATE inherits the
# base model's, which is what is actually running and what tool calling needs.
FROM gpt-oss:20b
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384
PARAMETER temperature 0.6
